\section{Modules}{
 Give \code{ns}, the module's \code{\link[shiny:NS]{shiny::NS()}} or its id, and
the expression is left as written while its names are the module's:
\verb{$inputs.size} is \code{input$size} of the module, \verb{$vueStore.ui} the store
made with \code{vue_store(ns("ui"))} -- as \code{input$size} is inside
\code{\link[shiny:moduleServer]{shiny::moduleServer()}}. Without \code{ns}, the names are the page's, and a
store named the same in two instances of a module is one store.
